# Cell from playpick: mode=walk, boss=whisper, spec=mage:frost, style=auto,
# size=25, difficulty=heroic, view=1280x800, save=carried.
#
# Probe (2026-09-25-12.play) already showed 25/heroic are locked on this
# profile -- "1/2" on both dropdowns, "1 of 11 built rooms open here" -- because
# #273 means `carried` behaves like a fresh origin inside a single playbot
# invocation. Same precedent as the 2026-09-24 clear-mode session: walk on the
# setup screen's own default (10-normal) rather than block the cell.
#
# "walk" means the long way: no #hash shortcut, walked in from the front page,
# stopping once the target room (whisper, The Last Whisper, in `oratory`, past
# marrow's `spire` and the climb) is reached rather than pushing further.
# `style=auto` has never appeared in a ledgered session before this one --
# it taps the autocast toggle and otherwise plays like idle (no dodge, no
# approach), so this is also the first read on what inDanger looks like for a
# body that casts but never moves.
open
targets
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
targets
tap class:mage:frost
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot arrive-threshold
state

# threshold -> vigil -> spire (marrow, a real fight) -> climb -> oratory
# (whisper, the target). Generous budget; evening stops itself early
# (evening-stuck) if two rooms in a row go nowhere -- which would itself
# be worth reading given #271's known vigil bug.
evening auto 260 2
shot after-evening
state
says
bill
targets
ui
